WEBVTT

01:03.938 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:08.943
Ae-sun, that brat!

01:09.569 --> 01:11.571
-You brat!
-Mother!

01:11.654 --> 01:12.906
-I don't want him!
-Mother.

01:12.989 --> 01:14.783
Yang Gwan-sik? No, thank you!

01:14.866 --> 01:16.201
No, thank you!

01:17.160 --> 01:19.621
Damn her! Ae-sun, that brat!

01:19.704 --> 01:21.372
Grandma, why are you doing this?

01:21.456 --> 01:22.707
-Why?
-What?

01:24.542 --> 01:27.504
Why did you ruin her cabbages
in the first place?

01:27.587 --> 01:28.546
Why, you little!

01:29.464 --> 01:31.674
She said, "No, thank you."

01:53.822 --> 01:55.240
Barnacles and whelks.

01:57.492 --> 02:00.036
A fishmonger's son
and a haenyeo's daughter.

02:00.537 --> 02:01.704
Same difference.

02:02.872 --> 02:04.874
Am I a maid dating a prince?

02:26.646 --> 02:29.899
Just hanging out doesn't mean
we'll fall for each other.

02:30.483 --> 02:35.113
It's all part of business, you know,
so I could set up shop next to your store.

02:35.196 --> 02:37.532
It's not like I'm dying to get married.

02:39.951 --> 02:42.078
I wouldn't take you
even if they hand you over.

02:42.579 --> 02:45.081
You think I'm crazy?
Why marry a guy from the island?

02:45.165 --> 02:48.126
In any case, my roots are in Seoul.

02:48.209 --> 02:49.377
Gyeonggi Noodle.

02:50.086 --> 02:53.131
Your uncle runs Gyeonggi Noodle.

02:53.214 --> 02:54.799
Gyeonggi-do is practically Seoul.

03:00.805 --> 03:03.099
That damn sea swallowed up
my father and mother.

03:03.683 --> 03:05.894
Seeing the waves all around
makes me feel sick.

03:05.977 --> 03:07.312
You think I'd stay here?

03:07.812 --> 03:10.940
I will marry a man from Seoul,
no matter what.

03:11.024 --> 03:12.734
Not some guy from the island.

03:13.401 --> 03:16.738
Especially not a guy
who doesn't even know what "nostalgia" is.

03:16.821 --> 03:17.655
Never!

03:21.701 --> 03:25.205
You're as quiet as a mouse.
Why aren't you saying anything?

03:25.705 --> 03:28.208
I'd rather live
with a dolhareubang rock statue.

03:28.791 --> 03:32.128
Then take your hand out of my pocket
and put it in a guy's from Seoul.

03:52.607 --> 03:54.442
Give away your son if you want.

03:55.193 --> 03:58.738
It seems like you're okay
with giving him to that girl.

03:59.322 --> 04:02.242
-I'd never go against you, Mother.
-Oh, you wouldn't?

04:03.618 --> 04:05.245
You came to this family knocked up.

04:05.328 --> 04:08.206
Don't push them too hard.
It might lead to an accident.

04:08.289 --> 04:09.999
You know what I mean.

04:10.083 --> 04:12.627
I know. That's why I'm acting like this.

04:12.710 --> 04:15.922
If we leave them alone,
they might elope at night like you did.

04:16.422 --> 04:19.050
Your son will also be stolen
right under your nose.

04:19.133 --> 04:23.054
Are you saying I stole your son, Mother?

04:23.596 --> 04:28.518
Rumors on an island this small
bring nothing but trouble for us all.

04:28.601 --> 04:31.187
Why are you pretending
to be so understanding?

04:31.271 --> 04:34.148
He's just a boy.
They'll hang out for a bit and move on.

04:34.232 --> 04:35.733
Let them be.

04:35.817 --> 04:39.112
Once they've had enough, they'll stop.
Why let it get to you?

04:39.195 --> 04:40.863
You know there's nothing you can do.

04:41.364 --> 04:45.493
The men in the Yang family
have been fools for generations.

04:45.576 --> 04:49.497
They can't tell a snake from a rabbit.
And I'm the mean wench, they say.

04:50.873 --> 04:52.125
Leave them alone.

04:53.376 --> 04:56.337
People pity beggars. They don't love them.

05:09.517 --> 05:10.685
Is it mackerel today?

05:11.561 --> 05:13.771
Being pitiful is wonderful.

05:14.647 --> 05:16.357
My life is full of freebies.

05:17.900 --> 05:20.320
If it were out of pity, I'd feed a beggar.

05:21.112 --> 05:25.408
The school always gives me
the leftover powdered milk.

05:25.908 --> 05:27.201
Like I should be grateful.

05:28.453 --> 05:30.872
You think I gave you fish
for ten years out of pity?

05:31.414 --> 05:33.333
Then why did you give me them?

05:33.416 --> 05:36.210
You think I've spent ten years
as your minion out of pity?

05:36.294 --> 05:38.087
So why did you give me them?

05:38.796 --> 05:40.965
It's about time you told me why.

05:43.509 --> 05:45.261
What are you looking at?

05:45.345 --> 05:47.597
Look at me when you talk to me!

05:49.557 --> 05:51.684
You only ever feed me.
You never make a move.

05:52.393 --> 05:56.022
Did your grandma tell you to hand me fish
and keep your mouth shut?

05:56.606 --> 05:59.734
Did she tell you not to talk to me
in case we get involved…

06:06.616 --> 06:10.161
You little punk! You're such a brat.

06:14.165 --> 06:15.541
Do you kiss little punks?

06:15.625 --> 06:16.751
That was my philtrum!

06:16.834 --> 06:18.294
I wouldn't kiss a beggar either.

06:19.253 --> 06:20.088
Honestly,

06:20.755 --> 06:23.257
who says they like someone like that?

06:23.341 --> 06:24.801
I won't live with my grandma.

06:24.884 --> 06:26.010
I want to live with you.

06:27.970 --> 06:28.971
Seriously,

06:29.680 --> 06:33.226
who on earth would kiss the philtrum
and then say things like…

06:34.060 --> 06:35.353
So stop yapping!

06:35.436 --> 06:38.689
I don't know what happened to me.
I can't hear what you're yapping about.

06:38.773 --> 06:41.401
I can just see your yapping mouth.
What should I do?

06:41.484 --> 06:44.153
You're the selfish brat
who puts her hand in my pocket.

06:44.237 --> 06:46.447
-Why are your lips so shiny?
-I put something on!

06:46.531 --> 06:47.490
-Why?
-To be ready.

06:47.573 --> 06:48.408
What?

06:51.702 --> 06:54.914
I've been ready since I was 14!

07:17.186 --> 07:18.980
SASSY FIRST LOVE

07:19.063 --> 07:21.941
The Jeju Canola Flower Festival
has started again this year.

07:22.024 --> 07:23.776
Jeju Island is bustling with tourists

07:23.860 --> 07:26.904
who have gathered
to see the scenery of the canola flowers.

07:26.988 --> 07:28.239
Especially this year,

07:28.322 --> 07:31.617
a variety of events for couples
are capturing attention.

07:31.701 --> 07:34.745
Let's interview some of the visitors here.

07:34.829 --> 07:37.665
Hello. Is it okay
if I ask you a few questions?

07:38.166 --> 07:40.168
So you're here to see the flowers today.

07:40.251 --> 07:41.919
How do you feel about them?

07:44.005 --> 07:46.257
The flowers remind me of my first love.

07:46.340 --> 07:48.134
-First love. Of course.
-Yes.

07:48.718 --> 07:50.094
Go live with her, then.

07:51.846 --> 07:53.681
Hye-ran, that's dirty.

07:54.682 --> 07:56.642
Mom, was Dad your first love?

07:58.102 --> 07:58.936
Was he?

08:00.646 --> 08:02.815
I don't know. I forget.

08:04.692 --> 08:05.526
Your first kiss?

08:05.610 --> 08:06.444
Are you insane?

08:06.986 --> 08:08.821
That's our mom you're talking about!

08:09.489 --> 08:11.324
You must be out of your damn mind.

08:11.407 --> 08:12.533
Yeah, just get lost.

08:14.076 --> 08:15.453
The flower field is so pretty.

08:15.536 --> 08:17.830
-It is.
-Our Jin-hee is prettier than a flower.

08:17.914 --> 08:20.500
Did you know
canola flowers have a very strong scent?

08:22.793 --> 08:24.837
The scent is so strongly sweet.

08:25.963 --> 08:29.592
It gives you such a headache.
You feel like you might faint.

08:36.849 --> 08:37.683
I'm hungry!

08:38.309 --> 08:40.770
Why haven't you eaten yet?

08:41.687 --> 08:44.023
Can't you just get rid of this thing?

08:44.774 --> 08:46.734
Dinner will be ready in no time.

08:53.866 --> 08:55.993
Why would you watch something so boring?

09:01.123 --> 09:03.084
MARINATED CHICKEN

09:11.259 --> 09:12.093
Back then,

09:13.010 --> 09:15.221
if I'd known that spring was truly spring,

09:16.764 --> 09:19.850
I would've lived my life to the fullest.

09:21.602 --> 09:23.354
I still won't marry you.

09:28.067 --> 09:32.280
It's just that, you know,
today's training was so tough...

09:32.363 --> 09:33.698
Shut up and just walk.

09:59.599 --> 10:06.606
That bald young man
Commuting at eight o'clock

10:08.024 --> 10:15.031
I can't wait to see
If I'll see him again tomorrow

10:16.616 --> 10:19.952
Sun-nam was eating

10:20.536 --> 10:24.332
And now she's gone

10:26.000 --> 10:29.337
Sun-nam was eating

10:30.212 --> 10:33.883
And now she's hiding

10:33.966 --> 10:35.009
I found you!

10:37.386 --> 10:39.597
Spring is ever so fickle.

10:49.732 --> 10:52.151
Just as it starts to feel warm,
it turns cold.

10:54.737 --> 10:57.281
Just as it feels cold, it turns hot.

11:00.201 --> 11:02.745
It rushes at you so fast,
leaving you dazed.

11:08.250 --> 11:09.877
What did we do wrong?

11:11.087 --> 11:11.921
Min-ok.

11:16.050 --> 11:17.551
Morally speaking,

11:17.635 --> 11:19.303
I have never been married.

11:20.054 --> 11:23.099
At least my legal marriage record
is clean.

11:23.182 --> 11:24.016
Min-ok.

11:24.100 --> 11:27.687
Why should I have to take care
of your late wife's child?

11:28.396 --> 11:29.647
Are you serving a master?

11:29.730 --> 11:32.108
Why are you trying to save face?

11:32.191 --> 11:34.443
Come next year, you’ll--

11:40.408 --> 11:42.660
Are you serving a master or something?

12:03.889 --> 12:07.393
Mom, Jong-gu is your eldest grandson,

12:07.476 --> 12:09.729
even if he drains everything we've got.

12:09.812 --> 12:12.523
He'll perform your annual ancestral rites
after you're gone.

12:13.983 --> 12:14.984
What is it?

12:15.693 --> 12:16.944
Is something bothering you?

12:17.737 --> 12:19.155
So what if it is?

12:19.238 --> 12:22.324
You've cared for that family,
and now you want something from us?

12:24.118 --> 12:25.619
Grandma, don't you have a room?

12:27.079 --> 12:28.831
Do you all sleep and eat in that room?

12:28.914 --> 12:31.167
If your family is struggling like this,

12:31.250 --> 12:34.086
you should work at a factory
or something to help out.

12:34.170 --> 12:36.672
Why are you taking care of another family?

12:38.466 --> 12:40.634
Do they pay you enough for this?

12:41.260 --> 12:42.595
It's not to make a living.

12:42.678 --> 12:44.388
It's just to buy some snacks.

12:44.889 --> 12:45.848
And now what?

12:45.931 --> 12:47.349
Are you a literary girl?

12:47.433 --> 12:50.227
You want to go to a college
that even Jong-gu didn't attend?

12:52.271 --> 12:53.105
What?

12:54.273 --> 12:55.900
Do you want to go to college?

12:57.818 --> 13:01.071
Mom, do you have savings to give her
when we're in this state?

13:01.155 --> 13:04.450
Get that family to pay you as a maid
so you can go to college!

13:04.533 --> 13:06.452
Even if we had plenty of spoiled rice,

13:06.535 --> 13:08.954
we wouldn't give it
to a dog that ran away.

13:11.957 --> 13:13.209
Why did you take them down?

13:13.292 --> 13:15.169
They're not yours! Why did you do it?

13:15.252 --> 13:16.796
They're not even yours!

13:16.879 --> 13:20.716
You expect me to live with a picture
of his late wife hanging above my head?

13:21.717 --> 13:24.887
Sun-nam, Sun-bong. What were you doing
when she took down the picture?

13:24.970 --> 13:26.347
Are ice pops all that matter?

13:26.847 --> 13:28.849
See this girl playing politics?

13:28.933 --> 13:31.560
She's already acting sly
to win them over to her side!

13:32.394 --> 13:34.814
You shouldn't have only bought
four ice pops.

13:34.897 --> 13:36.232
Why would I buy five?

13:36.315 --> 13:38.400
Do I have to please
your late wife's kid too?

13:38.484 --> 13:40.611
-Min-ok.
-Forget it.

13:40.694 --> 13:43.280
Morally speaking,
you should show some decency.

13:43.364 --> 13:46.033
-Min-ok.
-Yeah, forget it.

13:46.742 --> 13:47.576
Give me my money.

13:47.660 --> 13:49.745
Then I'll leave,
even if you beg me to stay.

13:50.329 --> 13:51.163
Wait.

13:51.872 --> 13:53.749
You borrowed money from a child too?

13:54.583 --> 13:55.417
Min-ok!

13:56.085 --> 13:57.211
Would I ever do that?

13:57.294 --> 13:58.629
I would never--

13:58.712 --> 14:00.381
Give me my money for tuition.

14:00.464 --> 14:03.467
You said if I raised your kids,
you'd send me to college.

14:04.635 --> 14:05.678
I see.

14:06.720 --> 14:08.848
He looked after you
when you had nowhere to go.

14:08.931 --> 14:10.474
Now you want money too?

14:11.141 --> 14:13.352
Give me my money. You promised!

14:14.270 --> 14:17.231
I even sold those cabbages.
Why won't you pay me?

14:17.815 --> 14:20.609
You said you were too scared
of my mom to scam me!

14:21.235 --> 14:22.903
What's scary about a dead wife?

14:22.987 --> 14:25.030
He's scared of his kids
growing up so fast.

14:25.114 --> 14:26.198
Min-ok!

14:26.282 --> 14:29.869
Next year,
he'll have three kids of his own.

14:29.952 --> 14:31.954
Why would he pay your tuition?

14:32.705 --> 14:36.375
More importantly,
Yeom Byeong-cheol is dirt poor.

14:36.917 --> 14:40.963
Rumor has it that he's living with me
because he can't pay me back.

14:41.046 --> 14:43.048
-Na Min-ok.
-What? Damn you, Byeong-cheol!

14:50.806 --> 14:53.267
Don't you get it? He had you fooled.

14:53.851 --> 14:56.395
You're on your own now.

14:59.356 --> 15:01.859
Of course, you're on your own now.
What did you expect?

15:01.942 --> 15:04.194
DECEMBER 1967

15:04.945 --> 15:07.072
Everyone looks out for themselves in life.

15:07.573 --> 15:09.658
Right now, soldering is the best.

15:09.742 --> 15:13.037
They teach you a skill, feed you,
pay you, and make you a patriot.

15:13.537 --> 15:15.497
This is your best bet.

15:15.581 --> 15:18.584
It's also on the mainland,
just like you've always wanted.

15:21.337 --> 15:23.839
Grind for a few years,
finish the apprenticeship,

15:23.923 --> 15:25.925
and they'll pay you 15,000 won a month.

15:26.008 --> 15:29.678
Eat and sleep at the factory,
and you won't have to spend any money.

15:30.846 --> 15:35.017
So send us half the money every month.

15:35.517 --> 15:36.644
Every single month.

15:40.314 --> 15:42.691
The eldest grandson's debt is also yours.

15:42.775 --> 15:46.070
Jong-gu has to do well
for you to find a good husband.

15:48.739 --> 15:52.451
It's better to be born a cow
than to be born a woman in Jeju.

15:54.536 --> 15:56.246
That's what my mom said.

15:58.415 --> 16:01.585
Jong-gu has been holding
ancestral rites for your father.

16:02.169 --> 16:03.671
What would you know?

16:04.171 --> 16:06.173
Jong-gu's rice is getting cold.

16:06.256 --> 16:08.008
I'm not working at the factory.

16:08.717 --> 16:09.593
I won't go.

16:11.595 --> 16:14.515
I won't clean up after my siblings
or the eldest grandson.

16:15.474 --> 16:16.308
No one.

16:16.392 --> 16:18.352
If you don't work, where will you go?

16:18.435 --> 16:22.147
You want to live in this tiny house
just to add to our troubles?

16:22.690 --> 16:25.234
I won't. I won't do any of it.

16:25.317 --> 16:27.945
If I keep living this way like a fool…

16:29.947 --> 16:31.281
it'll make my mom cry.

16:34.535 --> 16:35.369
Ae-sun,

16:36.662 --> 16:37.579
think about it.

16:38.372 --> 16:39.873
Your mom is gone.

16:41.458 --> 16:42.292
Right?

16:42.876 --> 16:46.964
There isn't a warm spot waiting
to welcome you in the world.

17:12.406 --> 17:16.535
How many rooms do you have?
Can you win against your grandmother?

17:17.953 --> 17:20.414
You'd lose, wouldn't you?

17:22.124 --> 17:24.293
What happened? Who upset you this time?

17:24.376 --> 17:26.295
He told me to go to Busan.

17:27.004 --> 17:29.256
He told me to work at a factory!

17:29.339 --> 17:31.800
I don't have a home anymore.

17:32.593 --> 17:36.847
Sun-nam and Sun-bong
got won over with ice pops.

17:36.930 --> 17:39.850
My grandma's family is broke.

17:40.726 --> 17:44.897
There isn't a warm spot in the world
that will welcome me.

17:44.980 --> 17:47.858
The only person in the world
who cares about me at all

17:48.358 --> 17:50.611
is you, Yang Gwan-sik.

17:51.570 --> 17:52.488
So…

17:55.032 --> 17:57.159
Why should I?

17:57.242 --> 18:01.371
Why do I have to end up
with a guy from the island?

18:07.294 --> 18:09.213
This is a silent outcry

18:10.339 --> 18:12.925
A handkerchief of eternal nostalgia

18:13.008 --> 18:15.052
Waving toward the blue sea

18:15.719 --> 18:19.014
I will marry a man from Seoul,
no matter what.

18:19.098 --> 18:21.850
A pure heart flaps like…

18:23.018 --> 18:26.188
A pure heart flaps in the wind like waves

18:26.271 --> 18:29.441
Especially not a guy
who doesn't even know what "nostalgia" is.

18:29.525 --> 18:30.359
Never!

18:30.943 --> 18:32.611
The first man to hang…

18:33.946 --> 18:35.280
Oh, who could it be

18:36.115 --> 18:40.452
The first man to hang
A sad and sorrowful heart in the air

18:41.578 --> 18:44.331
So what if you know what "nostalgia" is?

18:45.082 --> 18:46.375
What about college?

18:46.458 --> 18:47.793
What about becoming a poet?

18:47.876 --> 18:49.503
What about the mainland?

18:52.297 --> 18:53.924
I can't give you everything.

18:56.426 --> 18:59.680
But one thing I will do for you,
no matter what.

18:59.763 --> 19:01.098
Come on.

19:01.682 --> 19:06.145
Can't you at least just say
you'll give me everything?

19:06.228 --> 19:09.731
Just tell me you will give me
the moon and the stars!

19:11.358 --> 19:14.236
How can I live with someone like this?

19:15.487 --> 19:17.322
I don't know. I can't lie.

19:18.782 --> 19:23.203
You'd actually lose to your grandmother,
wouldn't you?

19:30.210 --> 19:31.753
This is a silent outcry

19:31.837 --> 19:33.338
Shut up.

19:38.760 --> 19:40.387
This is a silent outcry

19:40.470 --> 19:42.055
Stop it already!

19:42.848 --> 19:45.100
A handkerchief of eternal nostalgia…

19:52.441 --> 19:56.862
FEBRUARY 1968

20:04.286 --> 20:05.787
You don't have to fight to win.

20:08.040 --> 20:10.584
Even if you're the pro wrestler
"The Headbutt" Kim Il,

20:11.084 --> 20:13.170
it's better to avoid than to fight.

20:44.076 --> 20:47.412
I might be running away,
but I must take what I'm owed.

21:23.782 --> 21:27.452
Your grandma might want
to put me behind bars.

21:44.136 --> 21:45.429
You won't regret this?

21:46.013 --> 21:47.723
Once we leave Jeju by boat,

21:48.390 --> 21:50.267
there's no backing down.

21:51.893 --> 21:52.894
Don't!

21:53.395 --> 21:55.647
There are no take backs in life.

21:57.190 --> 22:00.402
If your life and my life
join together as one,

22:00.485 --> 22:02.654
we stick it out together
whether we live or die.

22:06.325 --> 22:08.410
So if you're scared, walk away now.

22:10.078 --> 22:11.288
Just go back home!

22:15.542 --> 22:18.920
In all the 19 years of my life…

22:23.508 --> 22:24.968
I've never felt more excited.

22:34.061 --> 22:36.521
-How fast can you run 100 meters?
-Twenty-four seconds?

22:37.564 --> 22:38.815
Forget it. Let's go.

22:45.155 --> 22:47.699
Who can stop the spring that barges in?

22:47.783 --> 22:50.827
FEMALE RUNAWAY PREVENTION PERIOD

22:50.911 --> 22:51.870
Spring in Jeju

22:52.954 --> 22:54.498
always seems to come

22:55.457 --> 22:56.625
particularly early.

23:05.467 --> 23:08.804
To honor the bloodless May 16 Coup,
known as the Revolution of Spring,

23:08.887 --> 23:12.057
events are being organized
across the entire country.

23:12.724 --> 23:13.558
For this…

23:14.059 --> 23:14.893
That spring,

23:15.811 --> 23:19.356
their coup d'état was as ambitious
as their first voyage…

23:19.940 --> 23:23.652
Even as the nation faced the threat
North Korean Kim Shin-jo's team posed,

23:23.735 --> 23:25.028
the president decided to…

23:25.612 --> 23:28.198
…but it wasn't as revolutionary
as they'd hoped.

23:28.865 --> 23:29.908
Provincial ID.

23:33.495 --> 23:35.080
Provincial ID.

23:36.540 --> 23:39.167
Without any ID,
we'll assume you're with Kim Shin-jo.

23:41.128 --> 23:42.546
You said you were grown-ups.

23:42.629 --> 23:44.005
Let's see your IDs.

23:45.715 --> 23:48.009
Why are you sitting in the corner,
looking scared?

23:48.510 --> 23:49.594
What are you saying?

23:50.303 --> 23:51.221
I don't get it.

23:52.514 --> 23:54.099
Excuse me…

23:54.683 --> 23:55.725
You're minors, right?

23:56.852 --> 23:59.271
Sir?

24:00.522 --> 24:02.190
You kids are runaways.

24:04.067 --> 24:05.902
How did you end up with her?

24:06.403 --> 24:08.113
What are you saying?

24:08.613 --> 24:10.115
I have no idea what you mean.

24:11.283 --> 24:13.994
Kids today are so shameless.

24:14.077 --> 24:16.246
How dare you board this ship
by yourselves?

24:18.790 --> 24:20.584
-Then just throw us overboard.
-What?

24:23.128 --> 24:24.546
Throw us overboard here.

24:26.339 --> 24:27.549
What's with the attitude?

24:27.632 --> 24:30.927
Do you come from a wealthy family?
Is your father a politician?

24:33.638 --> 24:34.473
Throw us off.

24:36.808 --> 24:38.894
What? Who are you?

24:39.561 --> 24:40.395
What?

24:40.479 --> 24:42.147
What are you?

24:42.230 --> 24:43.565
Husband and wife.

24:46.067 --> 24:47.027
What?

24:47.861 --> 24:49.362
We're husband and wife.

24:51.698 --> 24:54.284
We're adults, so we got married.
How can kids get married?

24:54.868 --> 24:55.869
Let's go, honey.

25:22.604 --> 25:23.563
What are you?

25:24.231 --> 25:25.190
Husband and wife.

25:30.028 --> 25:31.571
What am I meant to do with these?

25:31.655 --> 25:34.115
Why are you being so rude to us?

25:34.699 --> 25:35.909
Are these even yours?

25:35.992 --> 25:37.994
Are Busan people always rude to customers?

25:38.078 --> 25:39.287
We're all adults here.

25:39.371 --> 25:40.539
Did you steal these?

25:40.622 --> 25:41.957
They are his grandmother's.

25:51.091 --> 25:52.259
I need to see some IDs.

25:52.342 --> 25:53.343
We left them behind.

25:53.843 --> 25:54.844
Yeah, right.

25:54.928 --> 25:56.721
I'm sure you left them behind.

25:56.805 --> 25:59.099
I was born in early 1949.

25:59.182 --> 26:00.267
Year of the Tiger?

26:00.350 --> 26:02.310
-Exactly.
-It's actually the Year of the Ox!

26:04.854 --> 26:06.773
What are these? Did you steal them?

26:08.191 --> 26:10.151
-Are you thieves?
-We're runaways.

26:18.577 --> 26:22.956
NAMPOJANG INN

26:23.039 --> 26:27.544
We have neither a provincial ID
nor a citizen ID.

26:28.295 --> 26:31.089
Our wallets were stolen,

26:31.923 --> 26:33.883
so we don't have anything.

26:36.094 --> 26:36.928
Take it out.

26:46.646 --> 26:49.316
Maybe we can get a room with this first.

26:50.734 --> 26:51.776
Probably not, right?

26:52.694 --> 26:55.405
Sort of like a pawn shop?

26:55.488 --> 26:56.489
Newlyweds?

26:58.033 --> 26:59.326
You look like newlyweds.

26:59.409 --> 27:01.161
Are you on your honeymoon?

27:04.998 --> 27:05.832
That's fine.

27:06.416 --> 27:07.667
You can pay us tomorrow.

27:08.251 --> 27:11.588
How generous of you!
Are we running a charity?

27:12.213 --> 27:14.341
Your wallets were stolen
on your honeymoon.

27:14.424 --> 27:16.176
You must be really upset.

27:19.429 --> 27:20.513
You'll give us a room?

27:23.224 --> 27:25.018
Don't let being robbed upset you.

27:25.810 --> 27:27.812
Busan folks are epically generous.

27:48.792 --> 27:50.669
You could try standing up to her.

27:51.586 --> 27:53.338
Is your grandmother that scary?

27:54.172 --> 27:55.507
I'm not scared of her.

27:57.092 --> 27:59.094
Does standing up to her
make you a bad child,

27:59.177 --> 28:00.970
but running away isn't as bad?

28:02.430 --> 28:04.391
I'm not scared of my grandma.

28:06.267 --> 28:07.102
Yeah, right.

28:10.522 --> 28:12.440
I'm scared she'd give you grief.

28:23.493 --> 28:24.327
Are you okay

28:25.078 --> 28:26.830
with giving up on athletics?

28:28.498 --> 28:30.041
I'm not even that good.

28:31.584 --> 28:33.420
I did it for the free milk and bread.

28:35.213 --> 28:36.214
What are you, a pig?

28:42.929 --> 28:45.056
You take the GED test.

28:46.683 --> 28:48.184
I'll work at the factory.

28:58.528 --> 29:01.281
Do you know
why I'm marrying Yang Gwan-sik,

29:01.364 --> 29:03.450
the lamest boy in all of Jeju?

29:07.620 --> 29:08.455
Steel.

29:10.039 --> 29:11.124
You're like steel.

29:14.169 --> 29:17.464
We may have hungry days,
but you'll never break my heart.

29:21.259 --> 29:23.553
Even if someone gave me
a gold or silver axe,

29:24.053 --> 29:25.430
the steel axe is mine.

29:26.431 --> 29:27.891
The steel axe is the real deal.

29:29.434 --> 29:32.020
Nobody would give you
a gold or silver axe anyway.

29:33.354 --> 29:35.190
The lamest guy for sure.

29:47.243 --> 29:48.411
You said we were married.

29:51.873 --> 29:53.124
Doesn't seem like it.

29:57.629 --> 29:59.589
This doesn't seem like it at all.

30:07.514 --> 30:08.473
Yang Gwan-sik.

30:14.062 --> 30:14.896
Excuse me.

30:28.159 --> 30:32.622
Why so happy? She stole all your rings.
She took your yellow dress too.

30:34.624 --> 30:37.961
You know, the woman at Gwan-sik's house,

30:38.545 --> 30:40.755
her gold frog was taken.

30:41.673 --> 30:44.342
She had both her gold frog
and her son taken.

30:47.220 --> 30:49.764
Is that why you're happy?
Do you find it amusing?

30:50.890 --> 30:53.643
The boy's grandmother almost fainted.

30:54.143 --> 30:55.395
Man, they're so bold.

30:56.145 --> 30:58.481
How did they even think
of running away to Busan?

30:58.565 --> 31:01.776
Rumor has it that they caused
quite a scene on that ship.

31:04.112 --> 31:07.282
They're saying
Ae-sun led the whole ruckus.

31:11.035 --> 31:13.788
Ae-sun is a bit of a romantic, isn't she?

31:13.872 --> 31:15.874
They're lovers on the run, so to speak.

31:15.957 --> 31:17.333
Does romance pay the bills?

31:17.834 --> 31:21.462
Once they get hungry,
they'll start resenting each other.

31:21.546 --> 31:23.381
So what if they're hungry?

31:23.882 --> 31:27.677
You know, at their age,
they'd be happy to just spend all day

31:27.760 --> 31:30.346
eating tangerines together
on a heated floor.

31:31.806 --> 31:32.640
Min-ok.

31:34.934 --> 31:35.768
Were you happy?

31:36.561 --> 31:39.188
I don't remember
having tangerines with you.

31:41.566 --> 31:42.400
Let's do it now.

31:44.068 --> 31:45.069
Hey, you there?

31:49.407 --> 31:53.286
Write down what she was wearing.
I heard she stole your clothes.

31:53.995 --> 31:55.371
Are you going after them?

31:55.455 --> 31:57.874
You're like a bounty hunter.
It's a good look for you.

31:57.957 --> 32:01.628
How are you going to find them?
You'll never find them.

32:03.004 --> 32:06.466
-Quit rambling and write it down.
-I don't know what she was wearing.

32:07.175 --> 32:08.009
What?

32:08.092 --> 32:10.845
I'm a door-to-door saleswoman.
I have tons of clothes.

32:15.642 --> 32:17.101
It's their first night.

32:18.645 --> 32:19.771
Shut your trap!

32:22.857 --> 32:24.067
Epically generous, right?

32:26.069 --> 32:29.155
This is the crown jewel of Busan.

32:30.573 --> 32:32.367
It'd be a shame if you didn't try it.

32:34.994 --> 32:36.913
Is this really all on the house?

32:38.289 --> 32:40.249
Well, Busan is a big city.

32:42.085 --> 32:43.544
The floor's all warm now.

32:44.253 --> 32:47.715
Enjoy a few glasses of this soju
and have a nice rest.

32:47.799 --> 32:50.635
If you lie on this heated floor
while tipsy,

32:51.552 --> 32:54.347
you'll melt like butter in a frying pan.

32:55.098 --> 32:57.725
But don't just melt right away.

32:59.811 --> 33:01.187
Take your time.

33:02.188 --> 33:04.691
Get busy, if you catch my drift.

33:07.026 --> 33:09.946
It is your first night, isn't it?

33:11.739 --> 33:15.451
Look at you!
You're both blushing. Get right to it.

33:15.535 --> 33:17.704
You've come to the right place.

33:17.787 --> 33:21.290
Even the most inexperienced men
leave this place as experts.

33:21.374 --> 33:22.542
Ma'am!

33:23.334 --> 33:24.168
Oh my.

33:24.794 --> 33:25.628
Mind yourself.

33:32.719 --> 33:33.553
Give it your all.

33:50.236 --> 33:51.446
Give it your all.

33:53.781 --> 33:54.991
Give it your all!

34:05.251 --> 34:07.837
Jaecheop-guk for sale.

34:09.714 --> 34:12.675
Jaecheop-guk for sale.

34:15.178 --> 34:17.638
Jaecheop-guk for sale.

34:19.724 --> 34:22.685
Yes, over here, please. It's really good.

34:31.652 --> 34:32.904
Is the bathroom clean?

34:33.988 --> 34:34.822
Clean?

34:35.406 --> 34:36.240
Yeah.

34:37.200 --> 34:38.534
It's usable.

34:41.037 --> 34:41.871
Wait.

34:42.455 --> 34:43.581
Did you do that?

34:53.049 --> 34:54.759
I think the screw just came loose.

34:57.887 --> 34:59.847
Just leave it, then.

34:59.931 --> 35:01.933
What if they ask us to pay for it?

35:03.184 --> 35:05.311
Busan folks are epically generous.

35:21.410 --> 35:23.412
BILL
TOTAL: 640 WON

35:23.496 --> 35:26.040
Didn't she say
everything was on the house?

35:26.124 --> 35:26.958
What?

35:30.628 --> 35:31.462
What's this?

35:32.130 --> 35:32.964
What is this?

35:34.382 --> 35:35.383
That hurt.

35:44.559 --> 35:45.393
What?

35:46.727 --> 35:47.562
What's wrong?

35:52.150 --> 35:53.359
What? What is it?

35:57.071 --> 35:58.072
What's wrong?

35:58.573 --> 36:00.199
-Our bags.
-What?

36:00.283 --> 36:02.118
-Where are our bags?
-Bags?

36:04.412 --> 36:05.454
No one else got robbed?

36:05.538 --> 36:07.665
Were there any strange guests?

36:07.748 --> 36:08.916
What are you trying to pull?

36:09.834 --> 36:10.835
Sorry?

36:11.836 --> 36:13.504
Quit joking around and pay up.

36:13.588 --> 36:16.799
Additional charges for room service
and for breaking the fan mount.

36:16.883 --> 36:18.718
The broken mount is the evidence.

36:18.801 --> 36:20.261
-Why would it be broken?
-Yeah!

36:20.344 --> 36:22.555
The thief entered in the dark and--

36:22.638 --> 36:25.099
We know! You broke the mount.

36:25.183 --> 36:26.601
We're certain it was you.

36:26.684 --> 36:27.518
Why us?

36:27.602 --> 36:30.313
One of the guests
might have seen something.

36:30.396 --> 36:31.397
-You could ask.
-Yeah.

36:31.480 --> 36:33.107
So they know
people get robbed in this inn?

36:33.191 --> 36:35.359
Well, maybe your wife saw something.

36:35.443 --> 36:36.527
-Yeah.
-Sorry?

36:37.570 --> 36:39.780
I never saw any bags at all.

36:40.615 --> 36:42.617
You came here empty-handed.

36:42.700 --> 36:43.701
On the house.

36:44.368 --> 36:45.620
-Hey.
-Yes?

36:45.703 --> 36:48.289
Did you see these guys with any bags?

36:50.708 --> 36:51.542
Wait, what?

36:53.211 --> 36:54.962
This came from one of the bags.

36:55.046 --> 36:56.505
Only this was left on the floor.

36:57.715 --> 36:59.800
You had no bags, so we took pity on you.

37:00.384 --> 37:01.969
Now you want us to give you one?

37:02.053 --> 37:06.390
I mean, yesterday, we took our key
after setting down our bag here.

37:06.474 --> 37:07.850
You must be really upset.

37:08.935 --> 37:11.729
Why don't we just call the police?

37:12.688 --> 37:13.856
Should we call

37:14.357 --> 37:16.734
and tell them these kids are runaways?

37:17.318 --> 37:19.320
Busan folks are epically generous.

37:20.613 --> 37:23.074
This is the crown jewel of Busan.

37:23.157 --> 37:25.493
It'd be a shame if you didn't try it.

37:26.577 --> 37:28.621
SPY AWARENESS PROMOTION PERIOD
BUSAN POLICE

37:32.667 --> 37:33.501
MISSING PERSONS

37:33.584 --> 37:35.294
YANG GWAN-SIK, MALE, AGE 19
HANDSOME

37:35.378 --> 37:37.088
OH AE-SUN, FEMALE, AGE 18
VIXEN-LIKE

37:38.256 --> 37:39.090
Yes.

37:43.678 --> 37:46.472
Ma'am, you may as well
look for a needle in a haystack.

37:47.139 --> 37:49.892
How will you find kids
who were determined to run away?

37:51.978 --> 37:54.188
I'm running out of coins, Mother.

37:54.272 --> 37:56.607
Stop telling me about your dreams.

37:56.691 --> 37:58.693
I have to go, okay? Bye.

37:59.610 --> 38:00.528
A conception dream?

38:04.490 --> 38:07.326
Why would the rooster kidnap the kids?

38:07.994 --> 38:11.247
Are you telling me
you want to eat chicken right now?

38:11.330 --> 38:13.082
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

38:13.165 --> 38:14.417
Newlyweds?

38:14.500 --> 38:16.127
Here's the chicken you ordered.

38:17.628 --> 38:18.504
Enjoy!

38:18.587 --> 38:20.131
Do you think I'm an idiot?

38:20.840 --> 38:22.591
Did you think you had me fooled?

38:22.675 --> 38:26.429
Why did you give us a room and alcohol
if we had no bags or money?

38:26.512 --> 38:27.596
Quit yapping.

38:28.556 --> 38:30.266
Let's call the police now.

38:30.850 --> 38:34.020
They'll call your mother in Jeju
and tell her to come here.

38:34.103 --> 38:35.688
I need to teach this girl a lesson.

38:35.771 --> 38:37.732
How did you know we were from Jeju?

38:43.112 --> 38:44.363
Go. Yeah, just leave.

38:44.447 --> 38:46.824
-I'll just think of it as bad luck.
-Hold on!

38:46.907 --> 38:49.618
How did you know that we're from Jeju?

38:50.953 --> 38:53.706
Should we call the police
and go over the details one by one?

38:53.789 --> 38:54.665
The boat tickets.

38:55.458 --> 38:57.710
You found them
in the bags you stole, right?

38:59.253 --> 39:00.087
You birdbrain.

39:00.671 --> 39:01.505
You birdbrain.

39:03.758 --> 39:04.633
My suitcase.

39:07.011 --> 39:07.928
Our bags!

39:08.429 --> 39:10.514
Give them back to us!

39:10.598 --> 39:12.558
They're all we have left.

39:14.477 --> 39:18.105
My mom's picture is in that suitcase.

39:18.189 --> 39:19.940
My suitcase.

39:20.024 --> 39:23.694
You kept the room warm,
kept pouring us drinks,

39:24.278 --> 39:27.448
and made us "melt like butter"
just to steal our bags!

39:27.531 --> 39:29.950
They stole all those towels too.

39:30.034 --> 39:32.495
SUBONGYONG SAUNA
NAMPO BARBERSHOP - JUNGANG SAUNA

39:33.245 --> 39:34.246
You thief!

39:35.414 --> 39:36.415
Thieving… bitch.

39:37.583 --> 39:38.417
Got any proof?

39:39.877 --> 39:41.170
You saw our boat tickets.

39:41.253 --> 39:42.463
So what if we did?

39:42.546 --> 39:43.798
Got any proof?

39:43.881 --> 39:44.715
Got any proof?

39:45.966 --> 39:47.635
Scram while we're still being nice.

39:48.469 --> 39:51.305
Or we'll sell you both to God knows where.

39:53.307 --> 39:55.184
Scram while we're still being nice.

39:57.978 --> 40:00.231
Those bags were all we had.

40:03.692 --> 40:06.195
That was the only picture I had of my mom.

40:08.155 --> 40:09.990
The gold frog was in there too.

40:12.284 --> 40:14.829
It's not like we're beggars or anything.

40:15.996 --> 40:18.707
We're like those kids in the fairy tale

40:18.791 --> 40:21.961
who were lured by breadcrumbs
and captured by a witch.

40:24.046 --> 40:25.339
I don't know what that is.

40:26.674 --> 40:28.134
Hansel and Gretel.

40:29.844 --> 40:30.928
Never heard of it.

40:34.098 --> 40:37.852
I always thought
they were the biggest idiots.

40:38.936 --> 40:40.896
They lost their minds over the food

40:41.730 --> 40:44.358
and had no idea
they were about to be devoured.

40:49.947 --> 40:51.532
What happened to those kids?

40:52.450 --> 40:53.451
Did they survive?

40:54.577 --> 40:55.536
Killed.

40:57.037 --> 40:58.122
The witch killed them?

40:58.205 --> 40:59.039
No.

41:00.541 --> 41:01.500
They killed her.

41:05.504 --> 41:06.755
The children threw…

41:08.924 --> 41:10.593
the witch into an oven

41:11.677 --> 41:13.137
and burned her alive.

41:14.763 --> 41:15.598
Ae-sun.

41:16.098 --> 41:17.141
They killed her,

41:18.517 --> 41:21.187
took all her silver, gold, and treasures,

41:22.605 --> 41:25.232
and lived happily ever after.

41:27.067 --> 41:27.902
Oh Ae-sun.

41:28.527 --> 41:30.529
Those kids were really something.

41:47.254 --> 41:49.465
It's all on the house.

41:49.965 --> 41:51.550
Busan folks are epically generous.

41:52.301 --> 41:54.428
Have a drink in this warm room,

41:54.929 --> 41:57.556
and you'll melt like butter
in a frying pan.

41:59.183 --> 42:00.935
This right here is--

42:01.018 --> 42:02.520
What happened to that?

42:04.021 --> 42:04.855
Damn it!

42:05.356 --> 42:07.566
Yesterday, some lunatics came in here

42:07.650 --> 42:09.276
and caused a total ruckus!

42:11.070 --> 42:13.405
-Let me climb on your back.
-Okay.

42:13.489 --> 42:14.323
Hurry.

42:15.074 --> 42:17.576
Those little punks came in here
and made us flip out.

42:18.369 --> 42:20.538
I wanted to throttle them,
but I let them go.

42:21.247 --> 42:22.748
We're decent folks, you know?

42:47.439 --> 42:48.357
What is it now?

42:51.068 --> 42:52.027
Excuse me.

42:53.862 --> 42:55.406
I don't need any more free stuff.

42:55.489 --> 42:56.323
That free stuff--

42:56.407 --> 43:00.202
If you get drunk, they'll rob you.
She said you'll melt like butter, right?

43:01.537 --> 43:02.454
What are you saying?

43:02.538 --> 43:05.457
Don't turn the lights off, no matter what.

43:22.725 --> 43:24.101
Why isn't that girl sleeping?

43:32.901 --> 43:35.112
Well, we're not making any money tonight.

43:37.031 --> 43:38.657
Charge her double for the soju.

43:54.590 --> 43:57.301
The gold frog and my mom's picture
come first, got it?

43:58.886 --> 44:00.554
We look for our stuff first.

44:00.638 --> 44:03.182
If we can't find it,
we take their cashbox, okay?

44:07.436 --> 44:08.896
We'd still be in the red.

44:08.979 --> 44:10.522
That gold frog is worth way more.

44:10.606 --> 44:12.399
It's not like we're stealing.

44:18.864 --> 44:20.824
It was all we had for our future, right?

44:24.078 --> 44:25.079
Gwan-sik.

44:26.163 --> 44:28.165
You're the head of our family now, okay?

44:36.715 --> 44:37.675
Honey.

44:43.097 --> 44:43.931
Honey.

44:50.396 --> 44:51.230
Let's go.

45:20.509 --> 45:21.343
It's not there.

45:22.219 --> 45:23.053
Not there.

45:41.155 --> 45:43.073
Don't do it. Get the cashbox.

45:44.366 --> 45:45.200
The cashbox.

46:43.967 --> 46:45.302
Let's just go.

46:45.385 --> 46:47.513
Let's go. I'll buy you another one.

47:07.032 --> 47:07.866
Hey!

47:09.451 --> 47:11.203
-The cashbox.
-Hey, lady!

47:11.286 --> 47:12.120
Put it down.

47:12.955 --> 47:15.290
-Right, 24 seconds.
-Put the cashbox down.

47:15.374 --> 47:17.376
-Damn it, you punk.
-Put the cashbox down!

47:17.459 --> 47:19.670
I swear I'll beat this girl to a pulp!

47:21.171 --> 47:23.674
I'm done for. Just go!

47:23.757 --> 47:24.925
Go!

47:25.008 --> 47:25.843
Just go!

47:25.926 --> 47:29.054
You want us to sell this girl to a place
where no one can find her?

47:31.014 --> 47:32.850
Lady, that's the pit of my stomach.

47:34.643 --> 47:35.644
My stomach.

47:36.562 --> 47:38.480
Put it down before I lose it.

47:38.564 --> 47:40.232
-Come at me.
-Put it down!

47:40.315 --> 47:41.608
Come at me.

47:46.864 --> 47:47.865
Okay, let up a bit.

47:47.948 --> 47:49.324
-I'm dying!
-Hey, be quiet.

47:50.033 --> 47:51.368
Put it down. Now!

47:51.451 --> 47:52.744
-Lady.
-Look at that punk.

47:54.162 --> 47:55.622
That's right. Just go.

47:56.206 --> 47:58.500
-Put it down!
-Run along just like that, punk.

47:58.584 --> 47:59.543
Off you go, punk.

48:00.544 --> 48:01.545
Go!

48:04.423 --> 48:05.591
Seriously!

48:05.674 --> 48:07.509
I told you to put it down, punk!

48:08.886 --> 48:10.137
That's right. There you go.

48:11.972 --> 48:13.891
What the hell is he doing?

48:22.482 --> 48:25.903
Mom's first love
was the karate master Choi Bae-dal.

48:28.780 --> 48:31.533
As for Mom,
she was the pro wrestler Kim Il.

51:24.372 --> 51:29.002
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS"

51:36.343 --> 51:38.762
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
